When I roll a character, my main concern with stats is carrying capacity. 
With a possible range of 500~1000gp, subtract 200 or so for armor, another 
200-ish basic survival inventory, and that leaves something like 100~600gp 
unencumbered loot hauling capacity.

A suit of leather weighs in at 150, so the minimum wouldn't even allow 
safely toting a single extra suit of armor for polypiling, cash, or just 
getting out of the hands of monsters that can wear armor.

As an arbitrary comfort level, I want about 300gp minimum loot hauling 
capacity, and I'll exercise if I don't have it. Otherwise toting loot around 
is a major redundant trip thing. And here, the exercise is used to reduce 
the amount of time spent.  I haven't done the math, but it might be 
calculatable to figure out how much exercise time vs how much trip time 
saved.

